A property of a const and null is typed by the const's own type, or by its value's
JSON kind when it has none: n, an int32 const, is *int32; f, an untyped true, is
*bool. Both were *string, which refused their payloads
(0049-MADR-remediate-the-2026-11-01-debugging-pass.md, G17).

